{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"B\n    \n      Two Parallel Routes — Left + Right Slots\n      Structure: /studio/[id]/layout.tsx with @leftPanel and @rightPanel. Transcript stays as a component inside @leftPanel (not its own slot).\n      Context: Same 4-context split (VideoData state/actions, Transcript state/actions). Layout provides all contexts.\n      Player: Lazy loaded inside @rightPanel. Controlled by VideoData context values.\n      Skeleton: @leftPanel/loading.tsx and @rightPanel/loading.tsx for route-level skeletons. Additional Suspense boundary around lazy Player.\n      \n        Pros\n          2 clean bundles — left panel vs right panel\n          Left panel layout stays natural (transcript + controls in one flex column)\n          Simpler routing — 2 slots instead of 3\n          Transcript still isolated via context, can become its own slot later\n          Matches the visual layout: sidebar | main\n        \n        Cons\n          Transcript not code-split from controls (both in @leftPanel bundle)\n          Less granular than 3-slot approach","choice":"b","id":null,"timestamp":1774769476715}
